#3707
The Breached Masonry~
An old wall has been opened from within by generations of enormous rats.
To the east, the city's later brickwork survives behind a rusted gate;
to the west, a fur-polished burrow vanishes under buried foundations.
Broken paving underfoot hints that this junction once belonged to a
street or cellar long before it became part of the drains.
