The Drowned Mooring~
The locked way opens onto a broad underground basin. Old mooring rings
and timber posts line a shelf of worked stone where a flat-bottomed
skiff can tie up. Beyond, black water swallows the foundations of walls
and arches. Pale fish gather near lanternlight and vanish whenever the
surface ripples without wind.
